I walk towards the fruit shops.
There are many fresh pineapples there.
A vendor looks at me and smiles.
He cuts a small piece of pineapple.
He gives it to me on the tip of the knife.
I take that piece.
I eat it.
It is very sweet.
I do not ask the price.
The vendor quickly says the price.
"One pineapple is sixty rupees," he says.
I like it.
"I want one pineapple," I say.
He takes a big pineapple.
He gives it to me.
I give sixty rupees.
I say thank you to the vendor.
I walk forward.
